1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Mission Control turns broad life areas into a calm weekly operating system.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:10,000
Capture a task the moment it appears—without stopping to organize it.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:14,500
Inbox keeps loose commitments visible until you are ready to decide.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:18,000
Give every task a real home: an area backlog or an outcome-focused project.

5
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,500
Areas connect projects, standalone work, waiting items, and routines.

6
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:29,000
Project boards make the next concrete actions—and their current state—obvious.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,500
Switch between board and list views without creating another system to maintain.

8
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:37,000
Keep observations, decisions, and next-review notes beside the work they inform.

9
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:41,500
Routines protect repeating practices without turning a missed day into overdue debt.

10
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:46,000
Protect broad area blocks with a flexible weekly rhythm.

11
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:51,500
When a block begins, Mission Control turns the plan into a focused execution queue.

12
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:55,000
Choose only one to three high-impact tasks. Now advances automatically.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,500
Weekly Review prunes noise, chooses the week, and protects enough slack for reality.

14
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:06,500
Plan less. Execute what matters. Adjust without rebuilding your week.

